1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,982
They were not looking for us. That is the first
thing, and the whole of the next fifty

2
00:00:14,002 --> 00:00:15,030
years turns on it.

3
00:00:15,429 --> 00:00:21,212
The Tollhouse Compact is a trading association of
nineteen species, about four thousand

4
00:00:21,232 --> 00:00:26,881
years old, that operates on a principle so simple
it took human diplomats a decade to

5
00:00:26,901 --> 00:00:32,750
believe it: *a market is cheaper than a war, always,
at every scale, without exception.*

6
00:00:32,770 --> 00:00:38,819
It has no military. It has never held territory. It
has been extinguished twice and rebuilt

7
00:00:38,839 --> 00:00:41,420
both times by the people who missed it.

8
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:48,648
In August of 2103 a Compact survey vessel, on a route
it had flown for nine hundred years,

9
00:00:48,668 --> 00:00:55,344
detected something that had not been there on the
previous pass: four hundred and eleven

10
00:00:55,364 --> 00:01:01,965
artificial objects in a system that had been
catalogued as *pre-contact, industrial, no

11
00:01:01,985 --> 00:01:02,650
traffic.*

12
00:01:03,049 --> 00:01:09,245
The Compact's rules for that situation are four
thousand years old and take up eleven

13
00:01:09,265 --> 00:01:15,460
words. *Approach slowly, transmit continuously,
offer first, and never arrive armed.*

14
00:01:15,859 --> 00:01:21,818
The broker's name has nine syllables and the human
record renders it as Ashet. It came

15
00:01:21,838 --> 00:01:27,865
aboard Dock One alone, unarmed, in a translucent
envelope of its own atmosphere, and it

16
00:01:27,885 --> 00:01:33,982
brought — because the Compact's protocol requires a
gift and because four thousand years

17
00:01:34,002 --> 00:01:40,238
of practice have made them extremely good at choosing
one — a functioning cure for a human

18
00:01:40,258 --> 00:01:40,795
disease.

19
00:01:41,194 --> 00:01:47,569
Not a cure the Compact had developed. A cure it had
synthesised in eleven days from broadcast

20
00:01:47,589 --> 00:01:53,619
medical literature it had intercepted on the
approach, for a rare neurological condition

21
00:01:53,639 --> 00:01:59,601
that Umbrella's own people had failed to crack for
forty years, and that affected about

22
00:01:59,621 --> 00:02:01,045
nine thousand people.

23
00:02:01,444 --> 00:02:06,511
The narrator notes that this was a deliberate
choice: not a cure for something large,

24
00:02:06,531 --> 00:02:11,598
which would have looked like a demonstration of
power, but for something small, which

25
00:02:11,618 --> 00:02:13,034
looked like *attention*.

26
00:02:13,555 --> 00:02:15,704
You are the authority here.

27
00:02:16,104 --> 00:02:22,539
I am an authority here. There are four hundred and
eleven others and you will meet nine

28
00:02:22,559 --> 00:02:23,874
of them this week.

29
00:02:24,275 --> 00:02:27,025
That is not what your own people say.

30
00:02:27,425 --> 00:02:34,694
No. It is what our constitutional instruments say,
and I have spent twenty years making

31
00:02:34,714 --> 00:02:40,474
the two converge, and you have arrived in
the middle of the argument.

32
00:02:40,875 --> 00:02:48,398
Ashet's report to the Compact, which was published in
the human record in 2119, contains

33
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:54,484
a line that four generations of human
historians have found unbearable.

34
00:02:55,004 --> 00:03:00,275
*The subject's species appears to be governed by a
single individual who is actively attempting

35
00:03:00,295 --> 00:03:05,286
to reduce his own authority and has been doing so,
unsuccessfully, for approximately forty

36
00:03:05,306 --> 00:03:10,020
years. I have not encountered this configuration
before. I recommend extreme caution:

37
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:14,474
a power that is trying to give itself away is the
most difficult kind to price.*

38
00:03:14,875 --> 00:03:20,696
The negotiation lasted four months and the narrator
will give you the shape of it, because

39
00:03:20,716 --> 00:03:26,407
it is the last time in this account that Albert
Wesker is the second most powerful thing

40
00:03:26,427 --> 00:03:28,224
in the room and he knows it.

41
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:34,764
The Compact wanted three things: a trade station in
the system, most-favoured terms on

42
00:03:34,784 --> 00:03:40,923
human biological science — which was, they said
without embarrassment, the finest they

43
00:03:40,943 --> 00:03:47,155
had encountered in nine hundred years — and an
undertaking that humanity would not arm.

44
00:03:47,555 --> 00:03:53,612
That last one was not a threat. It was a *sales
pitch*. The Compact's entire proposition,

45
00:03:53,632 --> 00:04:00,167
four thousand years refined, is that a species which does
not arm gets the Compact's protection,

46
00:04:00,187 --> 00:04:06,176
and the protection has held nineteen times in four
thousand years, and the two occasions

47
00:04:06,197 --> 00:04:09,044
it failed are in every Compact schoolroom.

48
00:04:09,564 --> 00:04:14,459
You have four kilometre hulls. You have a drive that
we did not sell you and that your

49
00:04:14,479 --> 00:04:19,546
physics did not produce. You have an organism in cold
storage at your ninth facility that

50
00:04:19,566 --> 00:04:21,375
I will not discuss in this room.

51
00:04:21,654 --> 00:04:26,895
We are not asking you to disarm. We are asking you to
stop, at the point you have reached,

52
00:04:26,915 --> 00:04:31,863
in exchange for four thousand years of accumulated
reasons why every species that did

53
00:04:31,883 --> 00:04:34,084
not stop is a ruin that we trade over.

54
00:04:34,925 --> 00:04:37,595
(very cold) And if we decline?

55
00:04:37,995 --> 00:04:42,650
Then nothing whatsoever happens, Director. That is
the part your people keep failing to

56
00:04:42,670 --> 00:04:47,433
hear. We do not punish. We simply do not shelter, and
in about ninety years the Veth will

57
00:04:47,453 --> 00:04:51,625
arrive, and you will discover what that means
without us standing between you.

58
00:04:52,024 --> 00:04:53,725
He accepted two of the three.

59
00:04:54,125 --> 00:05:00,296
The trade station was placed at the fourth Lagrange
point in 2104 and is still there.

60
00:05:00,316 --> 00:05:07,216
The science agreement made Umbrella, within a decade,
the largest single exporter of biological

61
00:05:07,236 --> 00:05:13,917
knowledge in nine hundred light years, and the narrator
notes that it also gave five species

62
00:05:13,937 --> 00:05:19,235
access to Aeterna and that the Compact's own
actuaries had to be rebuilt.

63
00:05:19,634 --> 00:05:21,064
He declined the third.

64
00:05:21,584 --> 00:05:28,730
I am not going to promise that my species will not arm,
because I am not entitled to promise

65
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:36,052
it. There are seven billion human beings, four hundred
thousand of them in the Free Territory,

66
00:05:36,072 --> 00:05:42,906
and about nine hundred of them build ships in orbit,
and I have spent forty years making

67
00:05:42,926 --> 00:05:45,555
it possible for them to refuse me.

68
00:05:45,834 --> 00:05:52,645
You are asking me to use an authority that I have
been trying to dismantle, in order to

69
00:05:52,665 --> 00:05:59,004
guarantee something for four hundred years, on
behalf of people who are not born.

70
00:05:59,615 --> 00:06:06,633
(very cold) You have been talking to me for four
months. Tell me honestly: is that a refusal,

71
00:06:06,653 --> 00:06:11,704
or is it the only trustworthy answer you
have had from this system?

72
00:06:12,105 --> 00:06:19,692
Ashet's reply was eleven words and it is carved, in
Compact script and in nine human languages,

73
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:22,335
on the wall of the station at L4.

74
00:06:22,855 --> 00:06:26,325
It is the first answer I have not
had to discount.

75
00:06:26,725 --> 00:06:32,732
The narrator will spend a page on what the Compact
actually did to humanity, because every

76
00:06:32,752 --> 00:06:38,559
account concentrates on the Veth and the Choir and
the wars, and the thing that changed

77
00:06:38,579 --> 00:06:40,435
people's lives was a market.

78
00:06:40,834 --> 00:06:48,139
The station opened in 2104 with nineteen species
trading on it. By 2107 there were four

79
00:06:48,159 --> 00:06:55,463
hundred human businesses on it, of which three
hundred and eleven were not Umbrella and

80
00:06:55,483 --> 00:06:59,336
eleven were one person with a
cargo allowance.

81
00:06:59,735 --> 00:07:05,832
What humanity sold: biological science, which the
Compact considered the best in nine

82
00:07:05,852 --> 00:07:12,021
hundred light years; music, which nobody had
expected and which four species developed

83
00:07:12,041 --> 00:07:18,426
an expensive habit for; and — this is the part every
human schoolchild learns — argument.

84
00:07:18,946 --> 00:07:24,034
You will not understand this and I have stopped trying
to explain it politely. Your species

85
00:07:24,054 --> 00:07:28,806
produces disagreement of a quality we have not
encountered. Not conflict. Conflict is

86
00:07:28,826 --> 00:07:33,689
common and cheap. *Formal structured disagreement*,
conducted in public, by parties who

87
00:07:33,709 --> 00:07:36,216
continue to trade with each
other afterwards.

88
00:07:36,495 --> 00:07:41,662
There are five species in the Compact who have paid,
in hard trade credit, to have human

89
00:07:41,682 --> 00:07:46,672
advocates argue their disputes. We have nothing
like it. Our disputes are resolved by

90
00:07:46,692 --> 00:07:47,026
price.

91
00:07:47,425 --> 00:07:55,192
The Compact's archive at L4 contains four thousand
years of trade law and, in a wing added

92
00:07:55,212 --> 00:08:03,325
in 2111, the complete proceedings of the Human Assembly,
translated, updated weekly, consulted

93
00:08:03,345 --> 00:08:04,710
by nine species.

94
00:08:05,110 --> 00:08:11,862
Umbrella earned nothing from it. It had no part in
it. Albert Wesker read the Compact's

95
00:08:11,882 --> 00:08:18,557
assessment of it in 2112 and, according to the Red
Queen's log, read it four times and

96
00:08:18,577 --> 00:08:21,049
then sat for twenty-two minutes.

97
00:08:21,449 --> 00:08:27,496
The narrator will now cover thirty-seven years in a
page, because this is a story about

98
00:08:27,516 --> 00:08:32,379
one man and because for thirty-seven years
the story is not about him.

99
00:08:32,778 --> 00:08:38,792
Humanity went out. Not in an exodus and not in an
empire: in about four hundred separate

100
00:08:38,812 --> 00:08:44,826
attempts, most of them badly funded, nine of which
failed with loss of life, and fifteen

101
00:08:44,846 --> 00:08:46,609
of which became something.

102
00:08:47,009 --> 00:08:52,997
The *Christina* made landfall in 2098 at a system the
catalogue calls Kiln and its people

103
00:08:53,017 --> 00:08:58,803
call, for reasons that involve a joke about a
welder, Ochoa. Mira Halder was its first

104
00:08:58,823 --> 00:09:04,744
elected administrator, and resigned after one term
because she said the job should never

105
00:09:04,764 --> 00:09:10,888
be held by the person who built the place, and then
spent forty years building other things

106
00:09:10,908 --> 00:09:13,859
and arguing with the people who
did hold it.

107
00:09:14,259 --> 00:09:20,529
Raccoon City sent nine thousand people. The Arcology
sent forty thousand, which was ten

108
00:09:20,549 --> 00:09:27,109
per cent of its population, and the Tuesday problem in
the Free Territory — the consequence

109
00:09:27,129 --> 00:09:33,472
deficit, the four-times suicide rate — fell by two
thirds inside a generation and nobody

110
00:09:33,492 --> 00:09:35,568
has ever entirely agreed why.

111
00:09:35,969 --> 00:09:42,347
The Progenitor lineage went out too. There were about
four hundred of them by 2110: Evelyn

112
00:09:42,367 --> 00:09:48,746
Marsh's family and the families of the eleven people
she had, after nine years of argument

113
00:09:48,766 --> 00:09:55,571
with the Directorate and the Hangzhou tribunal, been
permitted to offer it to. Mira Reiss-Marsh,

114
00:09:55,591 --> 00:10:01,685
who was twenty-one, went to Ochoa on the second wave
and did not tell anybody what she

115
00:10:01,705 --> 00:10:03,179
was for eleven years.

116
00:10:03,578 --> 00:10:05,298
And Umbrella stopped growing.

117
00:10:06,448 --> 00:10:13,323
Umbrella, audit. Nineteen territories. Nine million
four hundred thousand people under

118
00:10:13,343 --> 00:10:20,619
administration, out of a human sphere of twenty-seven
point nine billion. Umbrella's share:

119
00:10:20,639 --> 00:10:27,914
nought point nought nine per cent, and falling. One
hundred and forty-one thousand Absolute

120
00:10:27,934 --> 00:10:34,969
personnel remaining; the release programme is at
sixty-six per cent. Four million Points

121
00:10:34,989 --> 00:10:37,855
this quarter, the lowest since 2029.

122
00:10:38,446 --> 00:10:41,016
The lowest since 2029.

123
00:10:41,416 --> 00:10:42,542
(flat) Yes.

124
00:10:42,942 --> 00:10:44,632
Am I doing badly?

125
00:10:45,581 --> 00:10:52,524
(flat) You are doing something I have no measure
for. Your species is growing at a rate

126
00:10:52,544 --> 00:10:59,646
that has no precedent in my record. Your organisation
is shrinking, deliberately, at your

127
00:10:59,666 --> 00:11:06,529
own instruction. I pay for consequence and the
consequence is enormous and almost none

128
00:11:06,549 --> 00:11:09,169
of it is now attributable to you.

129
00:11:09,451 --> 00:11:16,918
(flat) In four hundred and eleven worlds, no host
has ever run this experiment. I would

130
00:11:16,938 --> 00:11:18,984
like to see how it ends.

131
00:11:19,384 --> 00:11:26,311
The narrator notes that in 2141 the Veth Hegemony
arrived thirty-nine years ahead of the

132
00:11:26,331 --> 00:11:32,074
Compact's estimate, and that it did not find
a single man with an empire.

133
00:11:32,474 --> 00:11:38,875
It found seven billion people spread across four
hundred worlds who had spent forty years

134
00:11:38,895 --> 00:11:45,008
learning how to argue, and one very old thing in a
black coat standing quietly at the

135
00:11:45,028 --> 00:11:49,554
back of the argument, who had been
waiting for them since 2103.
